<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade-July 28.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade-July 28.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data,</p>
<p>for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock</p>
<p>Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended</p>
<p>July 26</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     350	   1.33     589450  206.31   19.81</p>
<p>State Bank	   320	   1.23     604450  193.42   20.04</p>
<p>Telco		  385	   1.49     275850  106.20   20.18</p>
<p>TISCO		  210	   0.79     382400   80.30   19.62</p>
<p>Castrol		660	   2.59     121150   79.96   20.46</p>
<p>Sterlite	     225	   0.88     261200   58.77   20.39</p>
<p>Reliance cap	  75	   0.30     584700   43.85   20.86</p>
<p>Tata Tea	     385	   1.32     113550   43.72   17.88</p>
<p>Nestle		 280	   1.10     146250   40.95   20.48</p>
<p>Colgate		305	   1.20     116200   35.44   20.52</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 18.75 percent on an annualised basis against 25.75 percent in the previous carry forward account ended June 19.</p>
<p>Note :- BC - Book Closure</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-2659000</p>
